    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="17.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 17.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="298" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.6"/> hwa oðrum sceole<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.7"/> borh oððe bote æt woruldlicum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.8"/> þingu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, gelæste hit him georne ǽr oððe æfter.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="298" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf hwá oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> scyle borh oððe bote æt woruldlicum ðingum, gelæste hít hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> georne ǽr oððe æfter.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="298" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf hwa oðrum scyle borh oððe bote æt weorlðlicu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.2"/></hi> þingum, geleste hit him georne ær oððe æfter.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="299" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis alteri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.3"/> debitor est de plegiatione uel aliqua contingentium secularium emendatione, reddat ei sedulo prius aut postea.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="299" ed="#liebermann"/>[17, 3] Et si aliquis debet alteri pecuniam aut aliquid aliud, reddat aut ante<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.7-2"/> aut post<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.8-2"/> in proximo.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.9"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="299" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis cuiquam debet fideiussionem uel solucionem de seculari negotio, soluat illi uel cito uel sero.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="17.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="168" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf hwá oðrum scyle borh oððe bote æt woruldlicum ðingum, gelæste hít him georne ǽr oððe æfter.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="246" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa oðrum sceole borh oððe bote æt woruldlicum þingum, gelæste hit him georne ær oððe æfter.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="299" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn einer dem andern Geborgtes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.de.1"/> oder Bussgeld aus weltlichen Beziehungen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_17-3.lnote.de.2"/> schuldet, zahle er es ihm willig vor oder nach [dem Feste],</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone owes another a loan or compensation in secular matters, let him pay it to him willingly before or after [the feast],</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="169" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone owes another a debt or compensation in connection with secular matters, he shall render it to him readily either before or after [the festival].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="247" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone must pay a debt or compensation to another because of a worldly matter, he is to do so promptly before or after the feast.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="299"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_25-2">VI Atr 25.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 25, 2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="159"><label>repeated</label> <ref target="clause:VAtr_20">V Atr 20</ref> <quote>a passing demand by Wulfstan, repeated in three texts, that worldly debts not be settled on holy festivals</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="159"><label>repeated</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_25-2">VI Atr 25.2</ref> <quote>a passing demand by Wulfstan, repeated in three texts, that worldly debts not be settled on holy festivals</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-046">Cn 1018 15–15.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 25.2.; Robertson (p. 139) takes I Cn from B, which begins at ‘mæssedæg’ in 14.2, the earlier clauses being supplied from G; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 299, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">298</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">298</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scyle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scyle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">298</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weorldl. ð., gelæst <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weorldl. ð., gelæst Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alterius <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alterius K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">fügt Hk zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel added by Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ausradirt, am Rande später</hi> an̄ <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> r. ante annum aut prius in pro. <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erased, later in the margin an̄ Cb; r. ante annum aut prius in pro. S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sed <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sed added by Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">299</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. 18—18, 3 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Inst.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. 18—18, 3 lacking in Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">298</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Bürgschaft’ missverstehen Q Cons; <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. V Atr 20²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q Cons misunderstand this as ‘surety’; <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. V Atr 20²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_17-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wählt Q <hi rend="italic"><hi rend="spaced">contingentia</hi></hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi>) wegen Gleichklangs mit <hi rend="italic">þing?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Does Q choose <hi rend="italic">contingentia</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi>) because of its assonance with <hi rend="italic">þing?</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
